## 2.2 Aqueous synthesis of \(\mathbf{UiO-66-NH}_{2}\)
\(\mathrm{ZrOCl}_{2}{\cdot}8\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) \(\left(0.5\ \mathrm{g},\,1.55\ \mathrm{mmol}\right)\) , previously stored in a nitrogenfilled glovebox) and glacial acetic acid \(\left(1.86\ \mathrm{g},\,31.0\ \mathrm{mmol}\right)\) were added to a \(50{\-}\mathrm{mL}\) round bottom flask containing deionized (DI) water \(\mathrm{[0\mL]}\) . Then, 2-amino-terephthalic acid \(\left(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{BDC}{\mathrm{-}}\mathrm{NH}_{2}\right)\) , \(0.394\;\mathrm{g},\,2.17\;\mathrm{mmol})\) was added to the above solution mixture and stirred for \(10\;\mathrm{min}\) . The stirring was then stopped and the flask was connected to a water condenser and heated in an oil bath at \(100\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(24~\mathrm{h}\) . After cooling to room temperature, the resulting solid was filtered by suction, washed with DI water \(\left(100\mathrm{~mL}\times3\right)\) and methanol \(\left(100\mathrm{~mL}\times3\right)\) . The crude product was collected and stirred in methanol \((20~\mathrm{mL})\) at \(80~^{\circ}\!C\) for three hours to remove unreacted linker and modulator. The above step was repeated twice with methanol. The crystal solid was dried at \(50\,^{\circ}\!C\) to afford \(\mathrm{UiO-66-NH}_{2}\) .
## 2.3 Synthesis of UiO-66-HDI
2.3 Synthesis of UiO-66-HDIA \(50{\-}\mathrm{mL}\) Schlenk tube charged with \(\mathrm{UiO-66-NH}_{2}\) powder \((500~\mathrm{mg})\) was connected to a \(\mathrm{N}_{2}\) -manifold. A mixture of N,Ndimethylformamide (DMF, \(10~\mathrm{\mL}\) ) and HDI \(\mathrm{[0\,\mL]}\) was bubbled with \(\mathrm{N}_{2}\) for five minutes and then transferred to the tube. The mixture was stirred under nitrogen atmosphere at \(80~^{\circ}\!C\) for \(24~\mathrm{h}\) . After cooling to room temperature, the resulting solid was collected by suction filtration and washed by DMF \(\left(100\mathrm{~mL}\times3\right)\) and dichloromethane \(\left(\mathrm{DCM}\right)\) \(\left(00\,\mathrm{mL}\times3\right)\) . The product was dried at \(50\,^{\circ}\!C\) to afford UiO-66-HDI as an off-white solid. To determine the percent functionalization, a sample of UiO-66-HDI \((5.0~\mathrm{mg})\) was digested by stirring with NaF \((2.0~\mathrm{mg})\) at \(70\,^{\circ}\!C\) in deuterated dimethyl sulfoxide \((\mathrm{DMSO})–u_{6}\) \(\left(0.5\ \mathrm{~mL}\right)\) , with a drop of DCl \((20\,\textrm{w t.}\%\) in \(\mathrm{D}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{\cdot}\) ) being added). Solution \(^{1}\mathrm{H}\) nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) analysis of the digested sample revealed ca. \(24.8\%\) ligand functionalization.
