## 2.5 General procedure for Knoevenagel condensation reaction of aldehydes and malononitrile
2.5 General procedure for Knoevenagel condensation reaction of aldehydes and malononitrileCatalysts \(\left(10\ \mathrm{mg}\right)\) were first placed in a glass vial. Then, malononitrile \((0.35\,\mathrm{\mmol})\) , benzaldehyde \((0.2\,\mathrm{\mmol})\) , and DI water \((0.5\mathrm{~mL})\) were added to the vial. The mixture was screwcapped and stirred at room temperature \((23\ ^{\circ}\mathrm{C})\) for \(1\,\mathrm{~h~}\) . The resulting mixture was filtered by suction. DCM \(\mathrm{[1.0\mL]}\) was added to the reaction vial to extract the residual product and then poured into the filter paper under suction. The above extraction and washing steps were repeated 4 times. The organic filtrate (ca. 5 mL) was subject to rotatory evaporation at room temperature to afford the desired Knoevenagel product. The yield and selectivity were determined by solution \(^{1}\mathrm{H}\) NMR using durene as the internal standard and \(\mathrm{CDCl}_{3}\) as the solvent.
