## 4 Conclusions
In summary, we have developed UPy-rich hydrophobic MOF catalysts via postsynthetic modification and realized extraordinary catalytic performance on the MOF coating. With the surface functionalization by UPy-PDMS, the MOFs show hydrophobicity while preserve its crystallinity. The control experiments demonstrated that the high catalytic efficiency of MOF catalysts originates from the synergy of basic UPy motifs and the hydrophobic polysiloxane spacers. The recycling test indicated the long-term stability of the UPy-PDMS-decorated MOFs for cycle use. Thanks to the processibility of supramolecular polymers, the modified MOFs have been further deposited on membrane supports, leading to a MOF coating with much improved catalytic efficacy in Knoevenagel condensation for less reactive substrates. This should be on account of the liquid superwetting and confinement effects. Moreover, the gram-scale tandem catalytic reactions for the chromene product demonstrate the industrial potential of the MOF coating. The combination of postsynthetic modification and liquid confinement effect in MOF catalysts can also be a universal strategy for other catalysis.
